{
  "_doc": "iOS visual QA scenes (docs/design/ios-visual-testing.md). nativeOnly (default: name starts with native-) = no -wgLocalMode, no driver. steps (tab | click | tag: give the first visible match a DOM id for a native tap | scroll: scrollIntoView that selector | settingsPage | file: put a picked file, content text (default {}), on that <input type=file> | consent: open that TrialConsent sheet | firstrun: open the W1 first-run picker over the seeded vault, or W2 with \"trial\" | invite: open the F1 \"Have an invite?\" sheet | offer: InviteSheet.offer(that claim URL), the P3 route | inviteRequest: open the W5 \"Request an invite\" sheet with a stub POST, \"sent\" also sends it) and ready (selectors that must be visible): the in-page driver (tests/visual/driver.js). native: XCUITest steps after #wg-qa-ready (ios/UITests): tap (DOM id or placeholder), type, clear, tapButton (label), waitFor (label or id), keyboard (wait for the software keyboard). Page scenes (Settings) open from Today first: a page keeps its origin tab lit, and each load restores the previous scene's tab, so without it Settings would light whatever ran before (med-e6ql). The page clock reads today 23:00 local (driver.js pinClock), so time-dependent text is stable. mask (optional): [{x, y, w, h}] fractions of the image that tests/visual/compare.mjs blanks before diffing (regions that still change run to run). localOnly: the cloud pass skips it. cloudOnly: the local passes (Playwright local, the iOS Simulator) skip it. platform (optional, \"ios\" or \"android\"): only that shell runs it (the first-run scenes are Android-only: iOS has no native first run since med-ta2n.17). args (optional, native scenes): extra launch arguments, a `-key` here replacing the base one (Dynamic Type; the Debug-only -wgQALock failed|cancelled, -wgQALoadError 503|404|local, -wgQAHoldMark). settings-erase-confirm, settings-replace-confirm and settings-delete-confirm only open their typed-confirm dialogs (they never type the word); journey turns gamification ON for the device, so it stays last. startHere ({drop: vault data sections, picked: W1 picks}) replaces the seeded vault with a partial copy and reloads, so today-start-here runs after every other scene. kitNudge (a kit-nudge status) answers the Today kit card's status read with it, for the rest of the run.",
  "version": 1,
  "scenes": [
